{number: 76}
{title: Work, for the Night is Coming}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Work, for the night is coming,
Work thro' the [F] morning [C] hours;
Work while the dew is sparkling,
Work 'mid [G7] springing flowers.
[C] Work when the day grows brighter,
Under the [F] glowing [C] sun;
Work, for the night is [F] coming,
When [C] man's [G7] work is [C] done.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Work for the night is coming,
Work thro' the [F] sunny [C] noon;
Fill brightest hours with labor,
Rest comes [G7] sure and soon.
[C] Give every flying minute
Something to [F] keep in [C] store;
Work, for the night is [F] coming,
When [C] man [G7] works no [C] more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Work for the night is coming,
Under the [F] sunset [C] skies;
While their bright tints are glowing,
Work, for [G7] daylight flies.
[C] Work till the last beam fadeth,
Fadeth to [F] shine no [C] more;
Work, while the night is [F] dark'ning,
When [C] man's [G7] work is [C] o'er.
{end_of_verse}
